jobs.description:
### **About Aivres**



Aivres is a leading global data center and cloud computing solutions provider committed to delivering innovative technologies that propel the world’s leading industries to new frontiers. We deliver and deploy robust, performance\-optimized, purpose\-built platforms to major data centers around the globe.



We are looking for a Hardware Engineer to join our Fremont office, CA.


### **Primary Responsibilities**


* Complete hardware product design, component selection, schematic design, and prototype debugging and testing according to project requirements;
* Review, verify, and confirm the design at different stages of product development;
* Collaborate with software engineers to complete hardware unit debugging and system function integration verification;
* Assist the factory in new product rollout and make design changes to address issues raised during trial production;
* Responsible for writing, organizing, and archiving product design, development, and testing related documents, and providing corresponding technical support.


**Qualifications**


* Major in electronics, electrical engineering, automation control, or computer hardware;
* Familiar with digital circuits, analog circuits, circuit analysis, microcomputer principles, CPLD/FPGA, etc.;
* Strong interest in hardware development, with strong learning ability, stress resistance, and communication and collaboration skills;
* Priority will be given to candidates with relevant hardware development internship or project experience in electronic systems;
* Priority will be given to candidates with experience using Allego, HFFS, Cadence, or similar EDA tools.

### **EEO Statement**



Aivres is an Equal Opportunity Employer and embraces diversity in our employee population. It is the policy of Aivres to provide equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status or special disabled veteran, marital status, pregnancy, genetic information, or any other legally protected status.


### **Details:**


* **Job Location:** Fremont, California, United States
* **Department:** R\&D
* **Job Type:** Full\-time, on\-site

**How to Apply:**
To apply, please send your resume to ushr@aivres.com.

